{
 "about": "D-SINK-82 and D-SINK-83 (the owner, 2026-11-05): two rules about the host a playlist chose, held in both mirrors by this one file (tests/test_provider_hosts.py runs the helper, tests/Model.test.js the model; neither is the oracle, this file is, and every expected value was written by hand). `firstEntry`: a guide hint that is a comma-joined list is read as its first entry, cut at the first `,` that is followed, after any run of the six ASCII delimiters, by a scheme and a URL's `://` (hint_first_entry / Model.hintFirstEntry). `noDot`: a host of one DNS label -- lower-cased, one trailing dot removed, no dot, not empty, not an IPv6 literal -- (dotless_host / Model.dotlessHost). `hintVerdicts`: Model.epgHintVerdict end to end, with what the helper's policy says of the same host when the shell sends `playlistHost` (DestinationPolicy.refuses_name; null when the first entry is not an http URL). `handOffs`: what the helper's guide fetch does with a URL a shell hands it (code, and every host it asked the resolver for); `listed` and `oneLabel` are the two predicates over it, which both mirrors answer. `absorbed` (the review's F1, 2026-11-06): an address the playlist chose that holds a raw `\"` or a `,` opening an attribute holding a URL, which no fetch sends (absorbed_attribute / Model.absorbedAttribute). `logoHosts`: the logo host the survey counts (logo_survey_host / Model.splitLogoUrl; \"\" is refused, never named) and what fetch_logo does with the URL.",
